<article class="env-lemma" id="0AGD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AGD">Lemma <span data-tag="0AGD">67.40.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[rr]_ h \ar[rd]_ f &  &  Y \ar[ld]^ g \\  &  B }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X \to B$ is a proper morphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$Y \to B$ is separated and locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then the scheme theoretic image $Z \subset Y$ of $h$ is proper over $B$ and $X \to Z$ is surjective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The scheme theoretic image of $h$ is constructed in Section <a href="/tag/082W" data-tag="082W">67.16</a>. Observe that $h$ is quasi-compact (Lemma <a href="/tag/073B" data-tag="073B">67.8.10</a>) hence $|h|(|X|) \subset |Z|$ is dense (Lemma <a href="/tag/082Z" data-tag="082Z">67.16.3</a>). On the other hand $|h|(|X|)$ is closed in $|Y|$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/04NX" data-tag="04NX">67.40.6</a>) hence $X \to Z$ is surjective. Thus $Z \to B$ is a proper (Lemma <a href="/tag/08AJ" data-tag="08AJ">67.40.7</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>